\title{recurSurvTests: recurrent survival and recurrent competing-risk reference methods}
\description{
\code{recurSurvTests} contains transparent reference implementations for recurrent
gap-time survival and recurrent competing-risk analyses discussed in the
Wang-Chang, Luo-Huang, and Sivadasan-Sankaran papers.
}
\details{
The package currently exposes recurrent survival, rank-test, and
competing-risk reference functions:
\itemize{
\item \code{\link[=wc_surv]{wc_surv()}} for a Wang-Chang / weighted-risk-set marginal recurrent
gap-time survival curve.
\item \code{\link[=psh_surv]{psh_surv()}} for the Pena--Strawderman--Hollander generalized product-limit
recurrent survival curve (the pooled gap-record Kaplan--Meier curve).
\item \code{\link[=wc_logrank]{wc_logrank()}} for the Luo-Huang \verb{G_rho*} two-sample rank test; \code{rho = 0}
is the recurrent gap-time log-rank analogue.
\item \code{\link[=ss_rcif]{ss_rcif()}} for the Sivadasan-Sankaran recurrent cumulative-incidence
estimator.
\item \code{\link[=ss_rcif_equal_causes_test]{ss_rcif_equal_causes_test()}} for a subject-bootstrap Wald reconstruction
of the equal-cause recurrent cumulative-incidence test.
}
}
\section{Data convention}{

Input data are in long format with one row per observed gap. Within each
subject, rows are in episode order. The final row is the right-censored gap
(\code{status = 0}), while all preceding rows are completed recurrent events
(\code{status = 1}). \code{gap} is a gap duration rather than calendar time. For
recurrent competing-risk analyses, \code{cause} is defined on completed-event
rows.
}

\section{Important implementation note}{

These are research reference implementations assembled from published
formulas. In particular, the equal-cause RCIF test is explicitly a bootstrap
reconstruction rather than claimed byte-for-byte reproduction of unpublished
author software.
}

